@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# Any live session token works as a bearer (D29): the seeded smoke session (SMOKE_SESSION_TOKEN),
# or the `token` returned by "Exchange the cookie session for a bearer" below.
@token = {{$dotenv SMOKE_SESSION_TOKEN}}

### Request a sign-in link (D22)
# With MAIL_PROVIDER=console the link is printed to the API log; open it in a browser
# (or GET it here) to receive the gobbit_session cookie.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/magic-link
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "you@example.test" }

### Who am I (cookie or bearer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Exchange the cookie session for a bearer (D30; cookie-authenticated requests only)
# Send it with the browser's cookie, e.g. `Cookie: gobbit_session=<value>`; a bearer request gets 403.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token-exchange

### Sign out this session
# Careful: with the seeded smoke token this revokes it — re-run `pnpm db:seed` to restore it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sign out everywhere (revokes every session of the user, the smoke token included)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### OpenAPI schema
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json

### List decks
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get the test deck (create it below first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List test-deck categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List test-deck items in a category (page 1)
# The seed creates no decks or cards (D49): run "Create a new deck", "Create a category" and a few
# "Create a text item" requests below first; swap `food` for the category slug you created.
# @name foodPage1
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/items?category=food&status=published&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List test-deck items in the food category (page 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/items?category=food&status=published&limit=10&cursor={{foodPage1.response.body.nextCursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a new deck
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Deck",
  "slug": "test-deck",
  "kind": "personal",
  "isPublic": false
}

### Create a category in the test deck
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Category",
  "slug": "test-category",
  "visibility": "shared",
  "position": 0
}

### Create a text item in the test deck
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "text",
  "title": "Test Item",
  "body": "This is a test text item.",
  "payload": {},
  "categoryIds": []
}

### Get the created item
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update the created item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Test Item",
  "body": "Updated body"
}

### Archive the created item (D131; 409 invalid-transition on a proposal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restore the archived item (D131; keeps verifiedAt, no-op on a published card)
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add the item to favorites
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}/favorite
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remove the item from favorites
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}/favorite
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete the created item
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recently deleted cards (D132; needs item.delete, last 30 days, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/items?status=deleted
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Undelete the item (D132; 410 undo-expired after 30 days, 422 if it lost its categories)
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/{{created.response.body.id}}/undelete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Negative test: body exceeds CARD_BODY_MAX (600 characters)
# Expects 400 problem+json with errors[0].path = body (body is 601 'a' characters)
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "text",
  "title": "Oversized Body Test",
  "body": "",
  "payload": {},
  "categoryIds": []
}

### List deck members (implicit owner first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invite a reader (D37)
# 201 for a new membership, 200 when resending to a pending member. With MAIL_PROVIDER=console
# the invite link is printed to the API log; opening it signs the invitee in and accepts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "reader@example.test", "role": "reader" }

### Remove a member (owner only; implicit owners and yourself → 400)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck/members/<userId from the members list>
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete the test deck (owner only; soft delete, slug becomes reusable — D50)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/decks/test-deck
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ─── Family cards (D63): one request per card type; the Reader shows them at /d/family ───
# Run top to bottom against the deployed API (@baseUrl = https://gobbit.niranhome.win/api).
# Image cards need a publicId already uploaded through the Cloudinary console.

### Create the Family deck
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Family", "slug": "family", "kind": "shared", "isPublic": false }

### Create the Food category
# @name familyFood
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Food", "slug": "food", "visibility": "shared", "position": 0 }

### Text card (markdown body, no raw HTML)
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "text",
  "title": "Shopping day",
  "body": "**Thursday** after school. Check the [list](https://example.com/list) first.",
  "payload": {},
  "categoryIds": ["{{familyFood.response.body.id}}"]
}

### Link card
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "link",
  "title": "Favourite souvlaki place",
  "body": "Order the pita gyros.",
  "payload": { "url": "https://example.com/souvlaki" },
  "categoryIds": ["{{familyFood.response.body.id}}"]
}

### Image card (publicId from the Cloudinary console)
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "image",
  "title": "Pantry layout",
  "payload": { "publicId": "<folder/your-uploaded-image>", "alt": "Pantry shelves" },
  "categoryIds": ["{{familyFood.response.body.id}}"]
}

### Table card
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "table",
  "title": "Weekly meal plan",
  "payload": {
    "columns": ["Day", "Lunch", "Dinner"],
    "rows": [
      ["Sunday", "Falafel", "Fish with rice"],
      ["Monday", "Lentil soup", "Roast chicken"]
    ]
  },
  "categoryIds": ["{{familyFood.response.body.id}}"]
}

### Calc card
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "calc",
  "title": "Recipe scaling",
  "payload": {
    "fields": [
      { "key": "servings", "label": "Servings", "default": 4 },
      { "key": "grams", "label": "Grams per serving", "unit": "g", "default": 120 }
    ],
    "expression": "servings * grams",
    "resultLabel": "Total grams"
  },
  "categoryIds": ["{{familyFood.response.body.id}}"]
}

### Search (D68–D71; why = text | semantic | both)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/search?q=shopping&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ask (D77; 503 without OPENROUTER_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, 30/hour per user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which day do we go shopping?" }

### ─── Ingestion (Phase 5) ───
# Needs an extraction provider (OPENROUTER_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY), else 503. Jobs run in
# the worker (`pnpm dev` starts it); proposals then show up in the deck's review queue.

### Share a link into a deck (D93; 202 { id, status }, 50/day per user)
# @name shared
POST {{baseUrl}}/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "deckId": "family", "url": "https://example.com/plumber", "text": "Our plumber, call before 9", "channel": "paste" }

### Share a photo (multipart, ≤ 3 `files`, each ≤ 8 MB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=gobbit

--gobbit
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="deckId"

family
--gobbit
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="note.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./note.jpg
--gobbit--

### Job status / debug view (D109: sharer or a deck publisher)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ingest/{{shared.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an ingest token (D99; the secret is returned once, max 5 live per user)
# @name ingestToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/ingest-tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "label": "My iPhone" }

### Share with the ingest token (only POST /ingest accepts it; channel is always `shortcut`)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{ingestToken.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Bin day moved to Thursday" }

### List ingest tokens (display prefix only, never the secret)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/ingest-tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoke an ingest token
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/me/ingest-tokens/{{ingestToken.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Review queue (D106; needs item.publish)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Review count (the header pill)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/review/count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Publish a proposal (mode new | update; createCategory adds the suggested category)
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/<proposedItemId>/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "new", "createCategory": false }

### Discard a proposal (soft-deletes it and removes the job's uploads)
POST {{baseUrl}}/items/<proposedItemId>/discard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Resend inbound webhook (D104; 404 unless email-in is configured)
# Signed by Resend (Svix headers), so it can't be sent by hand: an unsigned request is a 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/resend/inbound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "email.received", "data": { "email_id": "test" } }

### ─── Card media (Phase 6, 008) ───

### Sign a direct photo upload (D133; 503 without CLOUDINARY_URL, 60/hour per user)
# The browser then posts the file with these fields to `uploadUrl`; the secret is never returned.
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/media/sign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Link preview (D134; { preview: null } on any failure, 30/hour per user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/link-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://example.org/" }

### Public runtime config (D55)
GET {{baseUrl}}/config

### Share preview HTML (D58; 200 with the private page for anything not public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/s/<itemId>

### ─── Public communal deck (Phase 8, 016) ───

### Make a category public (D176; owner or maintainer; the slug never changes)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/categories/<categoryId>
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "visibility": "public" }

### Make the deck public (D176; owners only, 403 owner-required otherwise; 409 on the personal deck)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/decks/family
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isPublic": true }

### Public deck summary (D174; no auth, 600/hour per IP, the same 404 for anything not public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/family

### Public cards, newest first (only published cards in public categories)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/family/items?limit=20

### Public cards in one public category
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/family/items?category=food

### One public card (allow-listed fields only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/family/items/<itemId>

### Public search (D182; no auth, 120/hour per IP; semantic only within the anonymous embedding budgets, else text-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/family/search?q=water&limit=10

### ─── Activity log (Phase 8, 020) ───

### Deck activity, newest first (D188; owners and maintainers, 403 otherwise; keyset cursor)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/events?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One card's history (survives the card being purged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/decks/family/events?itemId=<itemId>
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
